==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|blestre|lang=fro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪstə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[bubble]] between the layers of the [[skin]] that contains watery or bloody fluid and is caused by [[friction]] and pressure, [[burn]]ing, freezing, chemical irritation, disease or [[infect]]ion.
# A swelling on a plant.
# {{medicine}} Something applied to the skin to raise a blister; a [[vesicatory]] or other applied medicine.
#* '''1819''', Lord Byron, ''Don Juan'', I.168:
#*: 'T is written in the Hebrew Chronicle, / How the physicians, leaving pill and potion, / Prescribed, by way of '''blister''', a young belle, / When old King David's blood grew dull in motion, / And that the medicine answered very well [...].
# A bubble, as on a painted surface.
# {{context|roofing}} An [[enclosed]] pocket of air, which may be mixed with water or [[solvent]] [[vapor]], trapped between [[impermeable]] layers of felt or between the [[membrane]] and [[substrate]].

